  "claim": "C-029",
  "text": "On the mini suites, the Nemotron ladder on Token Factory passes as many task runs as Nemotron 3 Ultra alone, for under a quarter of its dollars per task run.",
  "scope": "Both contestants on Token Factory, one task run per task and suite (seed 0), interleaved, on the same tasks, under a dollar cap (ADR 0044). The ladder is the `router` contestant with the policy `bench/policies/tokenfactory-ladder.toml`: Nemotron 3.5 Lightning reads, navigates and summarizes; Nemotron 3 Super edits and runs the tests; Ultra plans, reviews and takes over after an escalation; a reviewer from another family gives a second opinion. Ultra alone runs every step and reviews its own changes. Dollars are the ledger's, at the list prices in `registry/providers/tokenfactory.toml`, for every model call of the task run, the reviews included. Both contestants ran without local models, so step classification and summaries of tool output used the same heuristics on both sides. The evidence reports tokens, uncached tokens and minutes per task run for both, and the bill of every hosted bench run.",
